# Introduction

If you have a Medicare Advantage plan and are looking for mental health support in Houston, one of the first questions you may have is whether your insurance can be used for counseling.

**Yes, Riaz Counseling accepts certain Medicare Advantage plans.** However, Medicare Advantage coverage varies by plan, network, provider, and benefits. The best way to determine whether your specific plan is accepted and what your expected costs will be is to have your benefits verified before your first appointment.

This guide explains what Medicare Advantage can cover for mental health care, what to check before scheduling therapy, and how Riaz Counseling can help you understand your options.

## Key Highlights

- Riaz Counseling accepts **specific Medicare Advantage plans**, but coverage can vary by plan and provider.
- Medicare covers a range of outpatient mental health services, including psychotherapy and counseling.
- Medicare Advantage plans provide Medicare-covered benefits through private health plans and may include additional behavioral health benefits.
- Being enrolled in Medicare Advantage does not automatically mean every therapist or counseling service is in-network.
- Riaz Counseling recommends verifying your specific benefits before beginning treatment.

## Does Riaz Counseling Accept Medicare Advantage?

**Yes. Riaz Counseling accepts specific Medicare Advantage options.** The practice has also published information explaining that patients should contact its intake team to verify their individual coverage and benefits.

This distinction is important because Medicare Advantage plans are not all the same. Your coverage may depend on the insurance company, plan type, network, provider, and specific behavioral health benefits included in your plan.

Rather than assuming that your Medicare Advantage card guarantees coverage, ask Riaz Counseling to verify your benefits before scheduling ongoing sessions.

## What Is Medicare Advantage?

Medicare Advantage, also called **Medicare Part C**, is an alternative way to receive Medicare Part A and Part B benefits through a private Medicare-approved health plan.

Medicare Advantage plans may have their own provider networks, cost-sharing requirements, and additional benefits. CMS notes that Medicare Advantage plans provide Part B-covered mental health services and may offer benefits beyond what Original Medicare covers, including certain supplemental mental health services.

Because plans differ, two people with Medicare Advantage may have different coverage for the same type of counseling.

## Does Medicare Cover Mental Health Counseling?

Yes. Medicare covers a range of mental health services.

Medicare Part B covers outpatient mental health care, including individual and group psychotherapy with eligible Medicare-enrolled providers. It can also cover family counseling when the primary purpose is to support treatment.

Medicare.gov identifies outpatient mental health care as including services used to diagnose and treat conditions such as depression and anxiety.

Depending on the person's circumstances, Medicare may also cover other behavioral health services, including intensive outpatient programs, partial hospitalization, and certain substance use disorder services.

The important point is that **having Medicare coverage and having coverage for a particular provider are not necessarily the same thing**. Your specific Medicare Advantage plan determines how your benefits are administered.

## What Should You Check Before Scheduling Therapy?

If you have Medicare Advantage and are considering counseling, it can help to confirm a few details before your first appointment.

### 1. Is Riaz Counseling in your plan's network?

Ask whether the specific Riaz Counseling provider you want to see participates in your Medicare Advantage network.

Network participation can vary by plan and provider.

### 2. Are mental health services covered?

Ask what outpatient behavioral health or counseling services your plan covers.

Medicare Advantage plans must provide Medicare-covered Part A and Part B benefits, but individual plans can have different networks, costs, and additional benefits.

### 3. What will you pay?

Your plan may have a copayment, coinsurance, deductible, or other cost-sharing requirements.

Medicare.gov notes that costs for outpatient mental health services can vary depending on factors such as the provider, facility, and other insurance coverage.

### 4. Are there provider or referral requirements?

Some plans may have specific rules about choosing providers, referrals, authorizations, or network services.

Ask your insurance provider or Riaz Counseling's intake team about any requirements that apply to your plan.

## Can Medicare Advantage Cover Therapy for Depression or Anxiety?

Mental health treatment for conditions such as depression and anxiety may be covered when the service meets Medicare and plan requirements.

Medicare specifically lists outpatient mental health services for diagnosing and treating mental health conditions such as depression and anxiety. Covered services can include individual and group psychotherapy and certain family counseling services.

If you're experiencing emotional difficulties, a qualified mental health professional can help determine whether therapy may be appropriate for your situation.

